quran[13]{c,v,t}:
  36,28,"And after him, We did not send any army (of angels) from the heavens upon his people, nor were We to send down (any punishment to destroy them)."
  36,29,"There was just one blast, and they were extinguished (like burnt ashes)."
  36,30,"Alas! For the (defiant) servants! No messenger ever came to them, but they used to mock him."
  36,31,"Have they not seen how many generations We have destroyed before them, who would never return to them?"
  36,32,Yet they all will indeed be presented before Us?
  36,33,And a sign for them is the dead earth. We give it (fresh) life and bring the grain out of it so they eat from it.
  36,34,"We produce in it gardens of date palms and grapevines, and cause springs to gush out of it,"
  36,35,"so that they may eat from its fruits, which their hands did not produce. Will they not then give thanks?"
  36,36,"Glory be to Him, Who created all things in pairs from what the earth produces, from themselves, and from other things they do not know."
  36,37,And a sign for them is the night. We strip the daylight from it. And behold! They find themselves in darkness!
  36,38,"And the sun (constantly) moves upon the course appointed for it. That is the measured design of the All-Mighty, the All-Knowing."
  36,39,"As for the moon, We have (also) determined phases (for its motion and rotation) until it appears back (to the dwellers of the earth) like an old dry branch of a palm tree."
  36,40,"It is not allowable for the sun that it should (deviate from its orbit and) overtake the moon, nor can the night precede the day. And all of them (i.e. the stars and the planets) are moving in their respective orbits."
